{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-40333" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the polynomial $P(x)=-{x}^{2}(x+1)(x-2)(x+2),$ find the solution of $P(x)\\le 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033945/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7cacbb8bac372eb9a183074b4a909e522bfdb1b5387bbfdce838d2ac30f97c4"} {"question" "q-40333" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve the inequality $P(x)\\le 0,$ we need to find the values of $x$ for which the curve $y=P(x)$ lies below the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nThe roots of the polynomial $P(x)=-{x}^{2}(x+1)(x-2)(x+2)$ are $x=\\pm 2,x=-1$ and $x=0,$ where\n\n- $x=\\pm 2$ and $x=-1$ are simple roots, and\n\n- $x=0$ has multiplicity $2.$\n\nAlso, $P(x)$ is a quintic polynomial with a negative leading coefficient. So, we can graph the curve as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033945/assets/1fb947e6360139669bae0821e0de8460da53ead628f589998fab1ce442646cdf.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving $P(x)\\le 0,$ we look for the part of the curve that is below the $x$-axis or touches this axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x\\in [-2,-1]\\cup {0}\\cup [2,\\infty ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033945/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7cacbb8bac372eb9a183074b4a909e522bfdb1b5387bbfdce838d2ac30f97c4"} {"question" "q-40333" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033945/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7aef578144ffd30ca53da10d4c0d7d76292c2a740c13eeeef93f55261116c8f2"} {"question" "q-40333" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033945/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7cacbb8bac372eb9a183074b4a909e522bfdb1b5387bbfdce838d2ac30f97c4"} {"question" "q-40333" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\in (-\\infty ,-2]\\cup [-1,2]"] ["math" "x\\in [-2,-1]"] ["math" "x\\in [-2,-1]\\cup [0,\\infty )"] ["math" "x\\in [-2,-1]\\cup [2,\\infty )"] ["math" "x\\in [-2,-1]\\cup {0}\\cup [2,\\infty )"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033945/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7cacbb8bac372eb9a183074b4a909e522bfdb1b5387bbfdce838d2ac30f97c4"} {"question" "q-40333" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\in [-2,-1]\\cup {0}\\cup [2,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033945/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7cacbb8bac372eb9a183074b4a909e522bfdb1b5387bbfdce838d2ac30f97c4"} {"question" "q-40334" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given $P(x)={x}^{4}-{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2},$ solve $P(x)>0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033945/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7cacbb8bac372eb9a183074b4a909e522bfdb1b5387bbfdce838d2ac30f97c4"} {"question" "q-40334" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve the inequality $P(x)>0,$ we need to find the values of $x$ for which the curve $y=P(x)$ lies above the $x$-axis.\n\nFirst, we factorize the polynomial $P(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x) & ={x}^{4}-{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}({x}^{2}-x-2) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}({x}^{2}+x-2x-2) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(x(x+1)-2(x+1)) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(x+1)(x-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe roots of the polynomial $P(x)={x}^{4}-{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}$ are $x=-1,$ $x=0$ and $x=2,$ where\n\n- $x=0$ has multiplicity $2,$ and\n\n- $x=-1$ and $x=2$ are simple roots.\n\nSo, we can graph the curve as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033945/assets/c0756761d00b0805683e447d8cee3b657bbbe004a0a47da428927585037b06c2.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving $P(x)>0,$ we look for the part of the curve that is above the $x$-axis.\n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x\\in (-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (2,\\infty ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033945/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7cacbb8bac372eb9a183074b4a909e522bfdb1b5387bbfdce838d2ac30f97c4"} {"question" "q-40334" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033945/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7aef578144ffd30ca53da10d4c0d7d76292c2a740c13eeeef93f55261116c8f2"} {"question" "q-40334" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033945/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7cacbb8bac372eb9a183074b4a909e522bfdb1b5387bbfdce838d2ac30f97c4"} {"question" "q-40334" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\in (-1,0)\\cup (0,2)"] ["math" "x\\in (-1,2)"] ["math" "x\\in (-\\infty ,-1)"] ["math" "x\\in (-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (2,\\infty )"] ["math" "x\\in (2,\\infty )"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033945/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7cacbb8bac372eb9a183074b4a909e522bfdb1b5387bbfdce838d2ac30f97c4"} {"question" "q-40334" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\in (-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (2,\\infty )"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/