rested in solving $P(x)<0,$ we look for the part of the curve that is below the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x\\in (-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (0,2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033945/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7cacbb8bac372eb9a183074b4a909e522bfdb1b5387bbfdce838d2ac30f97c4"} {"question" "q-116407" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033945/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7aef578144ffd30ca53da10d4c0d7d76292c2a740c13eeeef93f55261116c8f2"} {"question" "q-116407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033945/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7cacbb8bac372eb9a183074b4a909e522bfdb1b5387bbfdce838d2ac30f97c4"} {"question" "q-116407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\in (-3,0)\\cup (2,\\infty )"] ["math" "x\\in (-3,2)"] ["math" "x\\in (-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (0,2)"] ["math" "x\\in (-\\infty ,3)"] ["math" "x\\in (0,2)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033945/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7cacbb8bac372eb9a183074b4a909e522bfdb1b5387bbfdce838d2ac30f97c4"} {"question" "q-116407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\in (-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (0,2)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033945/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7cacbb8bac372eb9a183074b4a909e522bfdb1b5387bbfdce838d2ac30f97c4"} {"question" "q-116439" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given $P(x)={x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2},$ solve $P(x)>0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033945/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7cacbb8bac372eb9a183074b4a909e522bfdb1b5387bbfdce838d2ac30f97c4"} {"question" "q-116439" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve the inequality $P(x)>0,$ we need to find the values of $x$ for which the curve $y=P(x)$ lies above the $x$-axis.\n\nFirst, we factor the polynomial $P(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x) & ={x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}({x}^{2}+2x-8) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}({x}^{2}-2x+4x-8) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(x(x-2)+4(x-2)) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(x+4)(x-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe roots of the polynomial $P(x)={x}^{4}+3{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}$ are $x=-4,$ $x=0$ and $x=2,$  where\n\n- $x=0$ has multiplicity $2,$ and\n\n- $x=-4$ and $x=2$ are simple roots.\n\nSo, we can graph the curve as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033945/assets/a357caad0365f296f87367ee4ac1000f1ea772d0d27650c8340d475ca742828b.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving $P(x)>0,$ we look for the part of the curve that is above the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x\\in (-\\infty ,-4)\\cup (2,\\infty ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033945/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7cacbb8bac372eb9a183074b4a909e522bfdb1b5387bbfdce838d2ac30f97c4"} {"question" "q-116439" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033945/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7aef578144ffd30ca53da10d4c0d7d76292c2a740c13eeeef93f55261116c8f2"} {"question" "q-116439" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14033945/state.json" "file_sha